>>>malloy
import "storms.malloy"
>>>markdown
# 2020 US Storm Events Analysis
I chose to analyze storm events as weather has always fascinated due to my experience growing up in Central Texas. The dataset is from Kaggle and entails NOAA Storm data from 2020, which was a year for powerful storms in the midst of COVID-19. In this notebook, the types of storms, whether geography plays a factor or not, human impact, and economic damage will be examined. Additionally, there is a deeper look at floods and tornadoes due to the damage that these particular storms can have.
>>>markdown
## Storm Types: Frequency vs Danger
The most frequent storm type is thunderstorm wind at 14,461, but it wasn't the most destructive. Read on to learn what the most destructive was in terms of property damage and deaths. 
>>>malloy

#Stormtypes - Top 10 most frequent storm types
run: storms -> {
  group_by: event_type
  aggregate: event_count
  order_by: event_count desc
  limit: 10
}
>>>malloy
#Most property damage by storm type
run: storms -> {
  group_by: event_type
  aggregate: total_damage_property
  order_by: total_damage_property desc
  limit: 10
}
>>>malloy
#Deadliest storm types
run: storms -> {
  group_by: event_type
  aggregate: total_deaths_direct
  order_by: total_deaths_direct desc
  limit: 10
}
>>>markdown
## Geography: Where did Storms Hit the Hardest?
Some states bore most of the storm events of 2020. Read on to figure out who and to see further analysis of storms in Texas, Oklahoma, and Kansas, who are often nicknamed Tornado Alley.
>>>malloy
#Geography - states with most storm events
# bar_chart
run: storms -> {
  group_by: state
  aggregate: event_count
  order_by: event_count desc
  limit: 15
}
>>>malloy
#Which storm type dominates each region?
run: storms -> {
  group_by: state, event_type
  aggregate: event_count
  order_by: state asc, event_count desc
  limit: 50
}
>>>malloy
#Texas county storm breakdown
run: storms -> {
  where: state = 'Texas'
  group_by: cz_name
  aggregate: event_count, total_deaths_direct, total_damage_property
  order_by: event_count desc
  limit: 20
}
>>>malloy
#Kansas county storm breakdown
run: storms -> {
  where: state = 'Kansas'
  group_by: cz_name
  aggregate: event_count, total_deaths_direct, total_damage_property
  order_by: event_count desc
  limit: 20
}
>>>malloy
#Oklahoma county storm breakdown
run: storms -> {
  where: state = 'Oklahoma'
  group_by: cz_name
  aggregate: event_count, total_deaths_direct, total_damage_property
  order_by: event_count desc
  limit: 20
}
>>>markdown
## Human Impact: Which Storms Hurt People the Most?
In this section, I looked at which storm type caused the most direct and indirect injuries and which single storm event was the deadliest. Direct injuries occur during the impact of a storm, while indirect injuries occur either before or after the impact of the storm.
>>>malloy
#Human Impact - direct vs indirect injuries by storm type
run: storms -> {
  group_by: event_type
  aggregate: total_injuries_direct, total_injuries_indirect
  order_by: total_injuries_direct desc
  limit: 10
}
>>>malloy
#Deadliest single storm event
run: storms -> {
  group_by: event_type, state, cz_name, event_begin_time
  aggregate: total_deaths_direct
  order_by: total_deaths_direct desc
  limit: 10
}
>>>markdown
## Economic Damage: The Cost of the 2020 Storms
This section talks about the states with the highest overall property damage and the single storm event that left the most economic destruction.
>>>malloy
#Economic Damage - States with highest property damage
run: storms -> {
  group_by: state
  aggregate: total_damage_property
  order_by: total_damage_property desc
  limit: 15
}
>>>malloy
#Single most destructive events
run: storms -> {
  group_by: event_type, state, cz_name, event_begin_time
  aggregate: total_damage_property
  order_by: total_damage_property desc
  limit: 10
}
>>>markdown
## Flood Analysis
People tend to think tornadoes cause the most damage, however, floods cause a great deal of damage as they're typically more frequent. Read on to learn about the different causes of flooding. 
>>>malloy
#Flood Analysis - most commmon flood causes
run: storms -> {
  where: event_type ~ r'flood'
  group_by: flood_cause
  aggregate: event_count
  order_by: event_count desc
}
>>>malloy
#States flooded most frequently
run: storms -> {
  where: event_type ~ r'flood'
  group_by: state
  aggregate: event_count, total_damage_property
  order_by: event_count desc
  limit: 15
}
>>>markdown
## Tornado Analysis
There were 923 tornadoes in 2020. This section reveals the states with the most tornadoes and the intensity of these storms on the F-scale. 
>>>malloy
#Tornado Analysis
#States with the most tornadoes
run: storms -> {
  where: event_type = 'tornado'
  group_by: state
  aggregate: event_count, total_deaths_direct
  order_by: event_count desc
}
>>>malloy
#Tornado Analysis by F-Scale
# bar_chart
run: storms -> {
  where: event_type = 'tornado'
  group_by: tor_f_scale
  aggregate: event_count, total_deaths_direct
  order_by: event_count desc
}
>>>markdown

